<section class="page-hero">
  <div id="ambient-canvas" class="ambient-canvas"></div>
  <div class="container page-hero-inner">
    <span class="eyebrow">Free Tool</span>
    <h1>Free Sitemap URL Extractor — Pull Every URL From a sitemap.xml</h1>
    <p>Paste a <strong>sitemap.xml</strong> and this <strong>free sitemap URL extractor</strong> turns it into a clean list of URLs you can copy or download as CSV, with optional last-modified dates. Works on sitemap index files too. No signup, nothing leaves your browser.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container contact-grid llms-tool-grid">
    <div>
      <form class="contact-form llms-form" id="se-form" onsubmit="return false;" aria-label="Sitemap URL extractor form">
        <div>
          <label for="se-input">Paste your sitemap.xml contents</label>
          <textarea id="se-input" style="min-height: 260px;" placeholder="<urlset xmlns=&quot;http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9&quot;>&#10;  <url>&#10;    <loc>https://example.com/</loc>&#10;    <lastmod>2026-10-01</lastmod>&#10;  </url>&#10;  <url>&#10;    <loc>https://example.com/about</loc>&#10;  </url>&#10;</urlset>"></textarea>
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="se-format">Output format</label>
          <select id="se-format">
            <option value="list">One URL per line</option>
            <option value="csv">CSV (url, lastmod)</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="se-filter">Only keep URLs containing (optional)</label>
          <input type="text" id="se-filter" placeholder="/blog/">
        </div>
        <div>
          <label style="display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center;font-weight:500;"><input type="checkbox" style="width:auto;flex:none;margin:0;" id="se-dedupe" checked> Remove duplicate URLs</label>
        </div>
      </form>
    </div>

    <div class="contact-info-card llms-preview-card">
      <div class="llms-preview-head">
        <strong>Extracted URLs</strong>
        <span id="se-status" class="llms-status">Waiting for input</span>
      </div>
      <pre id="se-output" class="llms-output" style="max-height:340px;">Paste a sitemap to extract its URLs.</pre>
      <div class="llms-actions" style="margin-top:14px;display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" id="se-copy">Copy</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-glass" id="se-download">Download .txt / .csv</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container llms-explainer">

    <h2>What This Does</h2>
    <ul class="service-points">
      <li><strong>Pulls every <code>&lt;loc&gt;</code></strong> from a <code>&lt;urlset&gt;</code> sitemap into a plain list, ready for a spreadsheet, a crawler or a redirect map</li>
      <li><strong>Reads sitemap index files</strong> — if the root is <code>&lt;sitemapindex&gt;</code>, it lists the child sitemap addresses so you know which files to paste next</li>
      <li><strong>Keeps <code>&lt;lastmod&gt;</code></strong> in CSV mode, so you can sort by the date each page was last changed</li>
      <li><strong>Filters by path</strong> — keep only URLs containing text such as <code>/blog/</code> or <code>/products/</code></li>
      <li><strong>Removes duplicates</strong> and counts what is left</li>
      <li><strong>Decodes XML entities</strong> — an <code>&amp;amp;</code> in the file comes out as a normal <code>&amp;</code> in the list</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>When Pulling URLs Out of a Sitemap Helps</h2>
    <p>A sitemap is machine-readable, which makes it awkward to read by eye. Once the addresses are a plain list you can paste them into a spreadsheet and count pages by folder, compare them with a crawl to find pages that are in the sitemap but not linked internally, or build a redirect map before a migration. It is also a quick way to see how many URLs you are really asking Google to look at.</p>
    <p>Sitemaps have size limits: a single file can hold up to 50,000 URLs and 50MB uncompressed, so large sites split theirs into several files listed in a sitemap index. If you paste an index here, the tool shows the child sitemap addresses instead of page URLs. Open each child file, paste it, and extract from there.</p>

    <h2>Sitemap URL Extractor FAQs</h2>
    <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top: 22px;">
      <details>
        <summary>Does this tool fetch my sitemap from a URL?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>No. Paste the contents. Browsers block most cross-site requests to other people's files, and pasting keeps your data off every server, including ours.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What if my sitemap is a sitemap index?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>The tool detects a <code>&lt;sitemapindex&gt;</code> root and lists the child sitemap locations. Each child file then needs to be pasted separately to get its page URLs.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can I get the last modified dates too?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>Yes. Switch the output format to CSV and each row will include the <code>&lt;lastmod&gt;</code> value when the sitemap provides one.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Does it work with compressed .xml.gz sitemaps?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>Not directly. Unzip the file first and paste the XML text.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is there a limit on how many URLs I can paste?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>The tool has no limit of its own. Very large files may feel slow in the text box, since everything runs in your browser.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Does this tool store or send my data anywhere?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>No. Everything is processed in your browser with JavaScript — nothing is uploaded, logged, or stored on any server, including ours.</p>
      </details>
    </div>

    <div class="cta-band" style="margin-top: 44px;">
      <span class="cta-orb cta-orb-1"></span>
      <span class="cta-orb cta-orb-2"></span>
      <h2>Want someone to act on what the sitemap shows?</h2>
      <p>Contomatix runs technical SEO audits and fixes the issues they find.</p>
      <div class="cta-actions">
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Get in touch</a>
        <a href="https://wa.me/<%= site.whatsappNumber %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-glass">Chat on WhatsApp</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

